OL,3,GNEWSAScot, 70, took 40 years to
OL,4,Across-stitch Bayeux Tapestry replica on
OL,5,Ahis daily commute
OL,6,
OL,7,FA replica Bayeux Tapestry
OL,8,Fcross-stitched by an Aberdeenshire
OL,9,Fpensioner over nearly four decades is
OL,10,Fbeing put on display at the same time
OL,11,Fas the real thing in London.
OL,13,FThe work of Ian Williams, 70, is about
OL,14,Fa third of the size of the 230ft
OL,15,F(70m)-long original and will be on show
OL,16,Fat the Market Street Hall in Macduff.
OL,18,FThe actual Bayeux Tapestry has been
OL,19,Floaned to the British Museum by France
OL,20,Funtil July 2027 and is going on public
OL,21,Fdisplay in London for the first time.
OL,23,APub: 09-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,430,420,260,160,0,100
